WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.121 --> 00:00:03.421
- I had nightmares, of course, for

00:00:03.421 --> 00:00:06.092
I would say, for a couple of months.

00:00:06.092 --> 00:00:09.527
Waking up thinking that
I'm still in the camps.

00:00:09.527 --> 00:00:10.694
I was so happy

00:00:12.875 --> 00:00:14.958
that I was in a real bed.

00:00:16.345 --> 00:00:19.512
(serious piano music)

00:00:22.186 --> 00:00:24.818
In order to have a little bit of pleasure,

00:00:24.818 --> 00:00:26.309
let's say, which is,

00:00:26.309 --> 00:00:28.400
there's not too much of it in the camps,

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:30.355
I made friends with two Polish kids.

00:00:30.355 --> 00:00:33.199
We didn't get too much sleep,
and we used to just get out

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:36.026
real early in the morning
because in the barracks,

00:00:36.026 --> 00:00:38.625
it was just crying and screaming,

00:00:38.625 --> 00:00:43.044
and praying, and it wasn't
unusual that a prisoner,

00:00:43.044 --> 00:00:45.951
who was laying next to
you, to go to sleep,

00:00:45.951 --> 00:00:47.667
when you woke up, they were dead.

00:00:47.667 --> 00:00:51.540
In any of these camps,
everything is so the same

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:55.455
day in and day out that when
anything unique happens,

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:58.126
that is not on the schedule,

00:00:58.126 --> 00:01:00.543
you always immediately try to

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:03.418
talk about it.

00:01:03.418 --> 00:01:05.119
Is this good news or bad news?

00:01:05.119 --> 00:01:08.688
One morning, we came out
and the first thing we saw

00:01:08.688 --> 00:01:12.339
was that there no guards
in the guard towers.

00:01:12.339 --> 00:01:16.411
So, we are sneaking between
the barracks towards the gate,

00:01:16.411 --> 00:01:19.244
and lo and behold, nobody's there.

00:01:20.623 --> 00:01:23.886
We get enough courage to go to the gate,

00:01:23.886 --> 00:01:27.064
and we notice there's a heavy
chain with a padlock on it,

00:01:27.064 --> 00:01:30.426
and it's a very, very, foggy morning.

00:01:30.426 --> 00:01:33.051
We are just dumbfounded.

00:01:33.051 --> 00:01:36.254
All of a sudden, there's a
break in the fog, like a mirage.

00:01:36.254 --> 00:01:38.900
All you see is two horses with a horseman.

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:41.980
As he's coming closer, one of
the Polish kids says to me,

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:46.138
"Look at his hat," and it was
a red star, a Russian soldier.

00:01:46.138 --> 00:01:49.082
He comes to the gate and he says,

00:01:49.082 --> 00:01:52.943
"I'm advance guard,
nobody can leave the camp,

00:01:52.943 --> 00:01:54.597
"because there all sorts of diseases,

00:01:54.597 --> 00:01:55.735
"you're full of lice,

00:01:55.735 --> 00:01:57.798
"and you haven't been
washed in four months."

00:01:57.798 --> 00:02:01.046
But he says, as he takes out his gun,

00:02:01.046 --> 00:02:02.318
shoots off the padlock,

00:02:02.318 --> 00:02:04.807
"Doctors will be coming,
medication will be coming,

00:02:04.807 --> 00:02:06.716
"food will be coming very shortly."

00:02:06.716 --> 00:02:07.855
So the three of us,

00:02:07.855 --> 00:02:11.571
as fast as our skinny legs can carry us,

00:02:11.571 --> 00:02:14.408
we go to every barrack in the vicinity,

00:02:14.408 --> 00:02:16.915
open up the door, in every
language that we know,

00:02:16.915 --> 00:02:19.397
just yelling, "We are free, we are free."

00:02:19.397 --> 00:02:22.585
And you'll never forget that moment,

00:02:22.585 --> 00:02:24.993
the sounds from the barracks.

00:02:24.993 --> 00:02:28.376
Those who are able to walk
out to the sunlight walk out.

00:02:28.376 --> 00:02:30.126
Those who can't walk,

00:02:31.557 --> 00:02:32.457
crawling out.

00:02:32.457 --> 00:02:34.877
I have to pass through a little area

00:02:34.877 --> 00:02:36.595
where there are little bungalows.

00:02:36.595 --> 00:02:39.275
This is where the SS
families who are staying,

00:02:39.275 --> 00:02:41.119
and they must have left in a big hurry,

00:02:41.119 --> 00:02:43.768
because I go into one of the bungalows,

00:02:43.768 --> 00:02:47.049
and I open up the closet,
there clothing in there.

00:02:47.049 --> 00:02:48.919
Open up the pantry,

00:02:48.919 --> 00:02:51.585
food, and then I go into the bathroom,

00:02:51.585 --> 00:02:54.502
and I turn on the water, hot water.

00:02:55.484 --> 00:02:59.651
Fluffy towels, shampoo, soap
I haven't seen for a year.

00:03:00.493 --> 00:03:03.410
I make a little victory dance on my

00:03:09.306 --> 00:03:10.723
prisoner uniform.

00:03:12.545 --> 00:03:16.712
Get in there and take my
first hot shower in a year.

00:03:17.662 --> 00:03:18.912
It's wonderful.

